<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title><![CDATA[Linklog]]></title><description><![CDATA[Linklog]]></description><link>https://github.com/mondain-dev/linklog</link><generator>RSS for Node</generator><lastBuildDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 23:08:48 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://mondain-dev.github.io/linklog/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title><![CDATA[There is massive synaptic pruning between birth and adulthood]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HMFzVwmXUAAv48g.jpg:large"></p><p>Yaron Meirovitch (@YaronMeirovitch) on X</p><p>Massive synaptic pruning between birth and adulthood: the nervous system gets simpler with age! Two-decade connectomic effort in Lichtman lab @harvard reveals how the order in which motor neurons activate decides which connections survive. @NatureNeuro 👉 https://t.co/RqDv6Ea3hM</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/YaronMeirovitch/status/2072068359164731869">https://x.com/YaronMeirovitch/status/2072068359164731869</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/thursday-assorted-links-559.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=thursday-assorted-links-559">Thursday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/YaronMeirovitch/status/2072068359164731869</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/YaronMeirovitch/status/2072068359164731869</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 16:02:28 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Some major city populations from 1854]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HMH0eK3WEAAXGMD.jpg:large"></p><p>Simon Kuestenmacher (@simongerman600) on X</p><p>Here are the populations of 100 European cities of major importance in 1854. Note that it doesn’t say biggest cities. Didn’t expect Naples so high up the list. Only London and Paris had over a million residents.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/simongerman600/status/2072206105199980882">https://x.com/simongerman600/status/2072206105199980882</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/thursday-assorted-links-559.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=thursday-assorted-links-559">Thursday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/simongerman600/status/2072206105199980882</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/simongerman600/status/2072206105199980882</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 16:02:28 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Samuel Hammond 🦉 (@hamandcheese) on X]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1941687232538013696/jN33mhMu_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Samuel Hammond 🦉 (@hamandcheese) on X</p><p>The AI boom is doubly upsetting to progressive economic commentators because it a) shows “financialization” was largely a macro story that eventually solved itself, and b) the boom is being driven by AI rather than their hoped-for “green transition”.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/hamandcheese/status/2071978243700257086">https://x.com/hamandcheese/status/2071978243700257086</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/thursday-assorted-links-559.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=thursday-assorted-links-559">Thursday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/hamandcheese/status/2071978243700257086</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/hamandcheese/status/2071978243700257086</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 16:02:28 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[The safety of mRNA vaccines]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(26)00512-X/abstract">https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(26)00512-X/abstract</a></p><p>source: <a hr